==Latin==

===Etymology 1===
Derived from {{m|la|querquētum||oak forest}}, from {{m|la|quercus||oak}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|querquētulānus}}

====Adjective====
{{la-adj|querquētulānus}}

# [[oak]]-[[forested]]; covered by an oak [[forest]]

=====Declension=====
{{la-adecl|querquētulānus}}

=====Usage notes=====
'''Mōns Querquētulānus''' is an old name of the [[w:Caelian Hill|Caelian Hill]], one of the seven hills of Rome.

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|la|Querquētula}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{m|la|querquētum||wood of oaks}}, from {{suffix|la|quercus|ētum|t1=oak-tree|t2=plantation {{non-gloss definition|or}} grove}}, following [[Auckland]], from {{m|enm|ak||oak}} + {{m|en|land}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|querquētulānus}}

====Adjective====
{{la-adj|querquētulānus}}

# {{lb|la|New Latin}} Of or pertaining to [[Auckland]], [[New Zealand]]
# {{lb|la|relational|New Latin}} [[Auckland]]

=====Declension=====
{{la-adecl|querquētulānus}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|la|Querquētula}}

